cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MDVP: Deterministic, Explainable Design-Quality Measurement for Web Interfaces"
message: "If you use MDVP in your research, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Nikita
    family-names: Evseev
    affiliation: Tixo Digital
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tixo-Digital/mdvp-cli"
url: "https://mdvp.dev"
abstract: >-
  MDVP measures the design quality of any live web page through four
  deterministic pillars — objective CSS/DOM metrics, perceptual color
  science (Oklab color distance and APCA contrast), Shannon entropy as a
  design-consistency proxy, and a registry of AI-pattern ("vibe-code")
  detectors — plus optional spec-relative compliance against a DESIGN.md
  file. Scoring is bit-identical for a given DOM snapshot, requires no
  trained weights or GPU, and runs locally via Puppeteer.
keywords:
  - design quality
  - css metrics
  - oklab
  - apca contrast
  - shannon entropy
  - ai-generated ui detection
  - design systems
  - static analysis
  - web accessibility
license: MIT
version: 1.31.3
date-released: "2026-06-02"
